   <Row ss:AutoFitHeight="1">
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="Number">1</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">GPIO</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">gpio_reg_wr_rd_test</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">Register Read/Write Validation</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">This test validates the GPIO register block by performing default value verification and write-read integrity checks across all 49 GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_39, plus interrupt, IO control, data output, and data input group registers). First, each register is read after reset and compared against its expected default value with bit 0 masked out. Registers in the reset-skip list or with no readable fields are skipped. Second, six distinct test patterns are written to each writable register and read back. The read-back value is compared against the expected value computed from the write mask, read mask, and default values. Registers in the write-read skip list, or those with no writable or readable fields, are skipped. The test passes only if all default value checks and all write-read checks succeed across all registers and all patterns.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. Apply hardware reset (hreset_n) to the GPIO register block to initialize all registers to their default values.&#10;2. Read each of the 49 GPIO registers (gp0_gpio_8 through gp0_gpio_39, plus interrupt raw status/clear, interrupt enable, interrupt status, IO control group, data output group, and data input group registers) and verify the read value matches the expected default reset value. Registers in the reset-skip list (indices 37-48, covering VRRW-type group registers) and registers with no readable fields are skipped. Bit 0 is masked out during comparison.&#10;3. For each of the six test patterns (0xFFFFFFFF, 0xAAAAAAAA, 0x55555555, 0xF5F5F5F5, 0xA5A5A5A5, 0xFFFF0000), perform the following:&#10;   a. Write the test pattern (masked with the write mask) to all writable registers, skipping registers in the skip list (index 32 and indices 37-48) and registers with no writable fields.&#10;   b. Read back each written register (masked with the read mask) and compare against the expected value. The expected value accounts for writable bits receiving the pattern and non-writable bits retaining their default values.&#10;4. Verify that all default value checks pass with zero failures.&#10;5. Verify that all write-read checks pass with zero failures across all six test patterns.&#10;6. Confirm the test reports overall PASS if no failures occurred, or FAIL if any register mismatch was detected.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">gp0_gpio_8; gp0_gpio_9; gp0_gpio_10</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">1. All 49 GPIO registers that are not in the reset-skip list must return their expected default values after reset (with bit 0 masked). 2. For each of the 6 test patterns, all writable registers not in the write-read skip list must read back the expected value computed from the write mask, read mask, and default value arrays. 3. The default value failure count must be zero. 4. The write-read failure count must be zero. 5. The test must report PASS (finish with 0) when all checks succeed.</Data></Cell>
    <Cell ss:StyleID="Data"><Data ss:Type="String">The addr_array declares 49 entries but only 3 register address macros are explicitly visible in the source file (gp0_gpio_8, gp0_gpio_9, gp0_gpio_10); the remaining 46 entries are populated via header includes. The skip_array skips index 32 and indices 37-48 for write-read tests (VRRW-type group registers at offsets 0x94-0xC0). The skip_rst_array skips indices 37-48 for reset value checks. Bit 0 (data_in field, RO type) is masked out during default value comparison because the GPIO pin level may not match the expected reset value if no external value is forced. The soft reset function is disabled in the source code. Each per-GPIO register contains fields: data_in (bit 0, RO), intr_raw_sts (bit 1, RO), intr_clr (bit 16, WO), pedge_intr_en (bit 17, RW), nedge_intr_en (bit 18, RW), level_sel (bit 19, RW), io_ctrl (bit 20, RW2, reset=1), dout (bit 21, RW2, reset=0). Bus interface is AHB with 32-bit address width. Reset signal is hreset_n (active low asynchronous).</Data></Cell>
   </Row>
  </Table>
